/zot
/zotui
/.local/
/orders/
/internal/zotui/worker/artifacts/*.gz

configs/zot.yaml
.env

# The configuration baked into a portable build (`-tags portable`). It usually
# holds credentials, and a portable binary is only as safe to ship as its keys -
# so the source of those keys must never be committed. The template beside it,
# portable.example.yaml, is tracked; the filled-in file is not.
internal/config/portable.yaml

# Go workspace files, if anyone creates one locally. zot has no local module
# dependencies, so a go.work here is only ever a personal experiment - and one
# that will cap the toolchain below what go.mod requires if its go line drifts.
go.work
go.work.sum
